  "title": "Public Company Boards and the CEO – A key relationship",
  "summary": "All agree that recruiting, selecting, evaluating and compensating the CEO is one of the most important roles independent Directors of public companies fulfill. Some would argue that it is the most important responsibility of the Board in that it is through the CEO that the Board exerts actual operational control of the business. With that background in mind, here are some comments and recommendations regarding those critical Board tasks.",
